---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalLayout from '@components/article/LegalLayout.astro';
import { buildCategorySchema, buildMeta } from '@lib/seo';

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Privacy policy',
  description:
    "How SleekDrops handles your data: consent-gated, privacy-friendly analytics, minimal first-party cookies and browser storage, an FTC-compliant affiliate disclosure, and zero data sold to advertisers.",
  pathname: '/privacy',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  {...meta}
  schema={buildCategorySchema('Privacy policy', '/privacy', meta.description)}
>
  <LegalLayout
    eyebrow="Legal"
    titleHtml="Privacy <em>policy</em>."
    updated="September 3, 2026"
    toc={[
      { href: '#summary',      label: 'Plain summary' },
      { href: '#scope',        label: 'Scope of this policy' },
      { href: '#data',         label: 'What we collect' },
      { href: '#how-we-use',   label: 'How we use it' },
      { href: '#cookies',      label: 'Cookies & tracking' },
      { href: '#affiliate',    label: 'Affiliate disclosure' },
      { href: '#ads',          label: 'Advertising partners' },
      { href: '#third-parties', label: 'Third-party services' },
      { href: '#newsletter',   label: 'Newsletter' },
      { href: '#retention',    label: 'Data retention' },
      { href: '#security',     label: 'Security' },
      { href: '#children',     label: "Children's privacy" },
      { href: '#rights-gdpr',  label: 'EU/UK rights (GDPR)' },
      { href: '#rights-ca',    label: 'California rights (CCPA)' },
      { href: '#do-not-sell',  label: 'Do Not Sell or Share' },
      { href: '#changes',      label: 'Changes to this policy' },
      { href: '#contact',      label: 'Contact us' },
    ]}
  >
    <div class="summary" id="summary">
      <strong>Plain summary</strong>
      We host on Cloudflare, we use privacy-friendly analytics only with your consent, we don't sell anything to advertisers, and we keep cookies and similar technologies, including local and session storage on your device, to a minimum: essential ones for your dark-mode preference and saved articles, plus analytics and advertising ones only if you opt in — advertising is off unless you switch it on. Most outbound product links are affiliate links — we earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. If you signed up for the newsletter you can leave any time with one click.
    </div>

    <h2 id="scope">Scope of this <em>policy</em></h2>
    <p>This policy explains how SleekDrops ("we," "us," "our") collects, uses, discloses, and protects information when you visit <strong>sleekdrops.com</strong> or any subdomain we operate, subscribe to The Daily Drop newsletter, or contact us. It does not cover third-party websites we link to — once you click an outbound link, the destination's privacy policy governs your interaction with them.</p>
    <p>By using SleekDrops you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.</p>

    <h2 id="data">What we <em>collect</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops is a static publication. The site itself stores no personal data about you directly. The following limited information is collected by services we rely on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host (Cloudflare) automatically logs IP addresses, user-agent strings, and request paths for security, abuse prevention, and performance — standard for any website. We do not access or analyse these logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> With your consent, we use <strong>DevTeam Analytics</strong> (and Google Analytics 4) for privacy-friendly product analytics, to understand which pages and deals are useful and which parts of the site people actually use. We record anonymous, aggregate events (page views; a small set of funnel interactions such as hero call-to-action clicks, deal-card clicks, outbound "View deal" clicks, and newsletter sign-ups; and how you interact with the site's own controls, namely switching between light and dark mode, using the share or copy-link buttons, opening an image full-size, and following a table-of-contents link) together with non-identifying context only: the screen name, page path, deal or post slug, brand, retailer, call-to-action label, placement, the heading of a table-of-contents link you follow, and whether you are reading in light or dark mode. Light or dark is the only thing we record about your display preference, and it is noted on each event so we can tell how the site is read overall. Each event also carries two randomly generated identifiers that exist purely to make the counts correct — one for the event itself, so a duplicate can be discarded rather than counted twice, and one for your current visit, so page views from one visit are grouped together. Personal data is stripped in your browser before any event is sent, so no email addresses, names, full search or query strings, or anything you type is ever collected; DevTeam Analytics and Google may derive approximate location (country/region) from your IP address. Nothing runs until you opt in, and we honour Global Privacy Control / Do-Not-Track signals automatically; see <a href="#cookies">Cookies &amp; tracking</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter.</strong> If you subscribe, we store your email address and (optionally) your first name with our mail provider, solely to deliver the newsletter.</li>
      <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> If you write to us, we receive whatever information you choose to put in the message — typically a name, email, and the content of your question.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not collect special-category personal data (health, biometric, political opinions, etc.), and we never knowingly collect data from children — see <a href="#children">Children's privacy</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="how-we-use">How we <em>use it</em></h2>
    <p>We use the limited information described above to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate the site, fix bugs, and keep things working;</li>
      <li>Understand which posts are useful (aggregate analytics only);</li>
      <li>Send the newsletter to subscribers who asked to receive it;</li>
      <li>Respond to questions submitted through the contact form;</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations and prevent fraud or abuse.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use your data for automated decision-making, behavioural advertising, profiling, or sale to data brokers. We do not train AI models on your data.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies &amp; <em>tracking</em></h2>
    <p>We use cookies and similar technologies, including local and session storage on your device. Without analytics consent we store only two first-party items besides your privacy choice (below), and neither of them is a cookie:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><code>sd-theme</code> — browser local storage. Remembers your dark-mode preference (kept until you clear your browser).</li>
      <li><code>sd-bookmarks</code> — browser local storage. Stores the article slugs you've saved (kept in your browser only; never sent to us).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We store your privacy choice (<code>sd-consent</code>) in your browser's local storage as an essential setting that never leaves your browser. If you opt in to analytics, four more items are written:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>An anonymous DevTeam Analytics device identifier in browser local storage (DevTeam Analytics does not use cookies).</li>
      <li><code>sd_sid</code> — browser session storage (not a cookie). Groups page views from a single visit so analytics counts sessions correctly. It is randomly generated, is never derived from you or your device, and is used for nothing else. Cleared when the browser tab is closed, and replaced after 30 minutes of inactivity.</li>
      <li>Google Analytics' own first-party measurement cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>), used to count visits.</li>
      <li><code>sd-exp</code> in browser local storage, which records only which version of a page layout or wording you were shown so we can compare them in aggregate.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>All four exist only to make the anonymous analytics you consented to countable — discarding a duplicate event, grouping one visit's page views, counting visits, and recording which layout you were shown — and none of them is used for advertising or for tracking you across other sites. No analytics load, and no analytics cookie or storage is written, until you accept; <code>sd_sid</code>, <code>sd-exp</code>, the DevTeam Analytics device identifier and Google Analytics' <code>_ga</code> cookies are deleted the moment you decline or withdraw, and both analytics tools stop measuring straight away — you do not have to reload the page. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do-Not-Track signal we treat it as a decline and never start. You can change your choice at any time from <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> in the footer.</p>
    <p>Affiliate networks (Amazon, Awin, CJ Affiliate, Impact, and similar) may set their own cookies on <strong>the destination retailer's domain</strong> once you click an outbound link. SleekDrops itself sets no advertising cookies.</p>
    <p><strong>Advertising is a separate opt-in, off by default.</strong> Unless you switch <strong>Advertising</strong> on under <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>, no ad script is requested and no advertising cookie or storage is placed on your device — a decline, an unanswered banner and a Global Privacy Control / Do-Not-Track signal are all treated the same way. If you do switch it on, Google AdSense is loaded and sets its own cookies and browser storage; see <a href="#ads">Advertising partners</a>. You can withdraw that choice at any time from <strong>Privacy preferences</strong> in the footer, and no further ad script will load.</p>

    <h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate <em>disclosure</em></h2>
    <p>In accordance with the United States Federal Trade Commission's 16 CFR Part 255 ("Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising"), we disclose the following:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>SleekDrops is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program and other affiliate programs (including Awin, CJ Affiliate, Impact, Sovrn Commerce, and Skimlinks). These programs are designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to participating merchants. As an Amazon Associate, we earn from qualifying purchases.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>When you click a product link on SleekDrops and complete a qualifying purchase within the retailer's cookie window, the retailer attributes the sale to us and pays us a small commission. <strong>The price you pay is the same whether you click our link or not</strong> — the retailer absorbs the commission out of their margin. We never see who you are, what you purchased, or your payment details. We only see that an order was attributed to SleekDrops.</p>
    <p>For full details on how we choose what to link to, our testing standards, and how affiliate links are labelled, see the <a href="/disclaimer">Affiliate disclaimer</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="ads">Advertising <em>partners</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops displays third-party advertising only to visitors who have switched <strong>Advertising</strong> on in <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>. Where ads are served, they come from the following partner; this policy will be updated to name any other network we add:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — uses cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to our site and/or other sites on the Internet. Users may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The consent banner is shown before any non-essential cookie or browser storage is placed, in compliance with the ePrivacy Directive and GDPR, and the ad partner is loaded only after an explicit opt-in — a decline, an unanswered banner and a Global Privacy Control / Do-Not-Track signal all leave it unloaded.</p>

    <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party <em>services</em></h2>
    <p>The following services may process limited data on our behalf:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (USA / global) — hosting, CDN, security. Privacy policy: <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a>.</li>
      <!-- TODO(privacy): confirm DevTeam Analytics' hosting/jurisdiction and add its privacy-policy URL before publishing — not verifiable from the codebase alone. -->
      <li><strong>DevTeam Analytics</strong> — privacy-friendly product analytics, used only with your consent to measure anonymous, aggregate usage. We strip personal data in your browser before sending, so raw page URLs and referrers never reach it.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (USA / global) - aggregate traffic measurement, loaded only with your consent and alongside DevTeam Analytics. We send page paths rather than full URLs so query strings never reach Google. Privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Email service provider</strong> — used to deliver The Daily Drop newsletter. Stores subscriber email addresses with appropriate Standard Contractual Clauses for international transfers where applicable.</li>
      <li><strong>Affiliate networks</strong> — Amazon Associates, Awin, CJ Affiliate, Impact, Sovrn, Skimlinks. These are not processors of your personal data on our behalf; they are independent controllers that may receive limited information (such as a referring URL and a cookie ID) when you click an outbound affiliate link.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter</h2>
    <p>If you subscribe to The Daily Drop, your email address is stored with our mail provider for the sole purpose of sending the newsletter. We use it for the daily newsletter and nothing else. Every email contains a one-click unsubscribe link. You can request deletion of your address at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a>.</p>
    <p>We do not share your email with affiliate partners, advertisers, or any third party other than the mail provider that delivers the newsletter.</p>

    <h2 id="retention">Data <em>retention</em></h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscribers:</strong> for as long as you remain subscribed, plus 30 days after unsubscribe (to honour deletion requests and prevent re-subscription errors).</li>
      <li><strong>Contact form messages:</strong> up to 24 months, then deleted.</li>
      <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained by Cloudflare per their default retention (typically 7–30 days).</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> aggregate-only data; retained up to 36 months.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect the limited personal data we hold — HTTPS in transit, encrypted storage at rest with our providers, and access controls on administrative tools. No method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure; while we strive to use commercially acceptable means, we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2 id="children">Children's <em>privacy</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the EU/UK). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> and we will delete it. This commitment is in line with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and the UK's Age-Appropriate Design Code.</p>

    <h2 id="rights-gdpr">EU/UK rights <em>(GDPR)</em></h2>
    <p>If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland, you have the following rights with respect to your personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of any personal data we hold about you (in practice: just your email, if subscribed).</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — ask us to limit processing in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests, including direct marketing.</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where processing is based on consent (e.g., unsubscribe from the newsletter).</li>
      <li><strong>Lodge a complaint</strong> with your local supervisory authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Our legal bases for processing are: <strong>consent</strong> (newsletter subscription, optional cookies), <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (operating the site, fraud prevention, aggregate analytics), and <strong>legal obligation</strong> (responding to lawful requests).</p>

    <h2 id="rights-ca">California rights <em>(CCPA / CPRA)</em></h2>
    <p>If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act ("CCPA") and California Privacy Rights Act ("CPRA") give you specific rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to know what personal information we collect, use, disclose, and (if applicable) sell or share.</li>
      <li>The right to delete personal information we have collected from you.</li>
      <li>The right to correct inaccurate personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to limit use and disclosure of sensitive personal information.</li>
      <li>The right to non-discrimination for exercising any of these rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell personal information in the traditional sense. See <a href="#do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share</a> below for details on what constitutes a "sale" under the CPRA and how to opt out.</p>

    <h2 id="do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My <em>Personal Information</em></h2>
    <p>SleekDrops does not sell your personal information for monetary consideration. However, under the broader definitions of "sale" and "sharing" in the CPRA and similar U.S. state laws, the use of certain analytics or advertising cookies may be considered a "share" for cross-context behavioural advertising. Those cookies are only ever set if you switch the matching category on in <strong>Privacy preferences</strong>, so switching <strong>Advertising</strong> off there is itself an opt-out.</p>
    <p>To opt out of any such sharing, or to exercise any other privacy right, email <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> with the subject line "Privacy Request." We honour the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal where technically feasible.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this <em>policy</em></h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law. When we do, we will update the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Material changes will be announced in the newsletter and on the homepage for at least 14 days.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact <em>us</em></h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy, or want your data removed? Email <a href="mailto:privacy@sleekdrops.com">privacy@sleekdrops.com</a> or use the form on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. We aim to respond within five working days, and within 30 days for any formal access or deletion request under GDPR or CCPA.</p>
  </LegalLayout>
</BaseLayout>
